subsys/pmci/pldm/serial_bridge: add a RISC-V RERI error-injection shell

Add a shell-driven RISC-V RERI (RAS Error-record Register Interface, v1.0)
error injector to the PLDM serial_bridge sample, so the hardware-fault ->
firmware -> BMC path can be exercised end to end on QEMU sifive_u.

This is the Zephyr (fault-injection) half of the RERI demo. It pairs with the
QEMU RERI error-bank device (patch 0012), which maps a standard RERI bank at
0x10080000 and wires its abstract RAS signal to PLIC source 50.

Changes
  * src/reri_regs.h (new)
      RERI v1.0 register map shared by the shell and the RAS handler: 64-byte
      header (vendor_n_imp_id / bank_info / valid_summary) + 64-byte error
      records (control_i / status_i / addr_info_i / info_i / suppl_info_i /
      timestamp_i), with the status_i / control_i bit-fields and the error-code
      (EC) / RAS-signal (disabled/low/high/platform) encodings from the spec.
  * src/reri_shell.c (new)
      "reri" shell command tree. Injection follows the architected mechanism
      only -- no private registers: it programs status_i / addr_info_i, then
      arms control_i.eid so the modelled hardware counts down, sets
      status_i.v=1, updates valid_summary and raises the RAS signal.
        reri sdram-ue [addr]  inject an uncorrectable SDRAM data error
                              (EC=SYSTEM_MEMORY_DATA, UEC, PRI=high, UECS=high)
        reri sdram-ce [addr]  inject a corrected SDRAM data error
                              (CE, PRI=low, CES=low)
        reri dump             dump the bank header + record 0
      MMIO access uses sys_read64/sys_write64 at DT_REG_ADDR(reri0).
  * boards/hifive_unleashed_fu540_u54.overlay
      add the reri0 node (compatible "sifive,reri", reg <0x10080000 0x80>,
      interrupt-parent &plic, interrupts <50 1>).
  * dts/bindings/sifive,reri.yaml (new)
      minimal binding for the "sifive,reri" compatible (reg + interrupts).
  * prj.conf
      CONFIG_SHELL=y. The shell console stays on uart0; uart1 remains the
      dedicated MCTP link, so the shell does not disturb the bridge.
  * CMakeLists.txt
      build src/reri_shell.c.

Verified: builds clean for hifive_unleashed/fu540/u54 (Zephyr v4.3.0, SDK
0.17.4); the generated devicetree exposes /soc/reri@10080000 with reg and IRQ,
CONFIG_DT_HAS_SIFIVE_RERI_ENABLED=1, and the "reri" command is registered in
the ELF (shell_cmd_reri / reri_cmds).
